---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { publicationPath } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About the Publication — Constraint Grammar"
  description="Publication provenance, source hierarchy, citation guidance, and document status for Constraint Grammar of Completed Intelligibility."
  sourceStatus="Publication provenance"
>
  <article class="prose about-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About this publication</p>
      <h1>One theory, several kinds of document</h1>
      <p class="lede">This site is a static digital publication of the Constraint Grammar of Completed Intelligibility. It keeps canonical theory, structural reference, explanatory companions, developmental and interpretive material, historical reconstruction, academic positioning, and the project’s wordless runtime visibly distinct.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Governing hierarchy</h2>
      <p>The mature theory distinguishes three levels that should not be collapsed:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Coordinate-generated form</strong> — the structural form constrained by a position in the 6 × 3 × 3 grammar.</li>
        <li><strong>Canonical crystallization</strong> — the preferred mature name used to identify that generated form.</li>
        <li><strong>Concrete manifestation</strong> — a particular linguistic, social, practical, or other realization that may instantiate the form.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Canonical source corpus</h2>
      <p>The static publication is generated from source files kept in the repository. The principal canonical sources are:</p>
      <ul class="source-file-list">
        <li><code>constraint_grammar_of_completed_intelligibility_final_monograph.txt</code> — mature monograph.</li>
        <li><code>coordinate_forced_atlas.md</code> — canonical 54-cell structural atlas.</li>
        <li><code>constraint_grammar_54_plain_language_expositions_final.txt</code> — canonical explanatory companion for the 54 positions.</li>
        <li><code>constraint_grammar_exhaustive_glossary.md</code> — authoritative terminology and distinctions.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Supporting documents include the intellectual history and academic disciplinary positioning texts. An earlier academic draft remains archival rather than the governing theory source.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Derived and developmental material</h2>
      <p>The Layman’s Edition, Five-Year-Old through Eighteen-Year-Old sequence, Venture Edition, and Mainstream Consequences essay are derived readings of the same framework. They are not substitute canonical theory texts.</p>
      <p>The Five-Year-Old source is preserved as its own authored gateway. Years Six through Eighteen are generated from the single developmental editorial master and remain intentionally outside the ordinary search index. Wordless is the reader-facing table of contents for that developmental path.</p>
      <p>The Sentence Receptacle is a conceptual prospect rather than an implemented analyser. It uses the sentence as a privileged observational window onto completed intelligibility without treating the sentence as the ontology of the theory.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Theorem Zero</h2>
      <p>Theorem Zero is the project’s wordless runtime and canonical substrate v1.0. It is published unchanged from its designated runtime source. Its role inside this publication is philosophical and experiential: it provides a lawful substrate in which pattern and completion can be encountered without first being stated as prose.</p>
      <p>Its presence does not by itself prove metaphysical necessity, psychological reality, empirical universality, or the exhaustiveness of the 54-position architecture.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Portable Knowledge Edition</h2>
      <p>The Portable Knowledge Edition is a plain-text study corpus for personal reading, search, indexing, and permitted AI-assisted study. It contains the principal canonical sources, research and provenance context, the Five-Year-Old and Layman editions, and the Venture and Mainstream essays.</p>
      <p>It is deliberately not a mirror of every web-only part of the publication: the later developmental sequence, Wordless, Sentence Receptacle, and Theorem Zero are not included.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Version and repository</h2>
      <dl class="metadata">
        <dt>Publication version</dt><dd>0.2.0</dd>
        <dt>Publication date</dt><dd>9 August 2026</dd>
        <dt>Repository</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/TitanicParker/persistence">TitanicParker/persistence on GitHub</a></dd>
        <dt>Public URL</dt><dd><a href="https://titanicparker.github.io/persistence/">titanicparker.github.io/persistence/</a></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>No personal authorship details are asserted here beyond what is explicit in the public repository context.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Suggested citation</h2>
      <p><cite>Constraint Grammar of Completed Intelligibility</cite>. Digital publication, version 0.2.0, 9 August 2026. <span class="break-anywhere">https://titanicparker.github.io/persistence/</span></p>
      <p>When citing a specific chapter, Atlas cell, Form, Glossary entry, developmental edition, runtime, or essay, use that page’s stable URL and identify its document status.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="reader-nav" aria-label="About related reading">
      <a href={publicationPath('research-status/')}>Research status</a>
      <a href={publicationPath('theory/')}>Formal theory</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
